cientific communication.</p></sec></ack><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garfield</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>English &#x02013; An International language for science, The Information Scientist, Dec 76</article-title><source>Essays of an Information Scientist</source><year>1977</year><volume>1</volume><publisher-name>ISI Press</publisher-name><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>20</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B2"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ofori-Adjei</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Antes</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Tharyan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Slade</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamber</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Have Online International Medical Journals Made Local Journals Obsolete?</article-title><source>PLoS Medicine</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>e359</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16942397</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pmed.0030359</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B3"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garfield</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The English language- The lingua Franca of international science</article-title><source>Scientist</source><year>1989</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>12</fpage><lpage>12</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loria</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Arroyo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Language and country preponderance trends in MEDLINE and its causes</article-title><source>J Med Libr Asso